# Hold a drum and the sixteen steps are yours. OCT- turns the marked step on or off.
# OCT+ moves to the next step. With no drum held, OCT- is still back and OCT+ is still excite.
# The bass is not a step row, so OCT- while it is held is still back.
seed 42
reboot
wait 200
expect lane0 256
expect lane1 256
expect lane2 0
expect lane3 21845
expect lane4 4369
expect lane5 2570
expect iamsec 0
expect iammask 65
expect iamdon 16
expect litkeys 1281
# The hat is held. OCT+ moves the mark off step 1. It does not excite.
key b3 down
wait 40
tap OCT+
wait 1600
expect iamsec 0
expect iammask 65
expect lane3 21845
# Step 2 was a rest. OCT- turns it on. The open hat keeps its own steps.
tap OCT-
expect lane3 21847
expect lane4 4369
expect iamsec 0
expect lane0 256
key b3 up
wait 40
expect iammask 65
expect litkeys 1281
# The key again. The mark is back on step 1, which was on, so it goes off.
key b3 down
wait 40
tap OCT-
expect lane3 21846
key b3 up
wait 40
expect iammask 65
# Excite writes patterns again. The steps that were written stay.
tap EDIT
wait 1600
expect iamsec 2
expect lane3 21846
# Nothing held: OCT- is back. The lift returns. The steps stay.
tap OCT-
wait 1600
expect iamsec 0
expect iammask 65
expect lane3 21846
# Back undoes the last writing, then the one before it, and the hat is the preset again.
tap OCT-
wait 1600
expect lane3 21847
tap OCT-
wait 1600
expect lane3 21845
expect lane4 4369
expect lane1 256
expect lane2 0
# The clap is written on its own. The snare stays, and letting go does not turn the clap on.
key b2 down
wait 40
tap OCT-
expect lane2 1
expect lane1 256
key b2 up
wait 40
expect iamdon 16
expect iammask 65
expect litkeys 1281
# Bass has no steps. OCT- while it is held undoes the clap.
key w1 down
wait 40
tap OCT-
wait 800
key w1 up
wait 1600
expect lane2 0
expect lane1 256
expect iammask 65
expect iamsec 0
# And with nothing held, OCT+ is excite again.
tap OCT+
wait 1600
expect iamsec 2
expect iammask 0x71
